<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Televisa started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Televisa started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- J.P. Morgan analyst Matthew Harrigan said on Wednesday he had started coverage of Grupo Televisa SA de CV with a rating of long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Grupo Televisa should now emerge as a consistent Mexican outperformer, albeit predicated on steady delivery of advertising growth and eventual market recognition of the Latin direct satellite business,&quot; he wrote in an analysis.</p>
<p>-- &quot;However, we do not think that the market will accord Televisa the 18 times-plus EBITDA multiples that the stock commanded pre-devaluation, and we are consequently refraining from an immediate buy rating.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's shares were up 1/4 to 25-7/8.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
